{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Alert text as the operator receives it (SNS, 2026-10-19): \"Bedrock spend-cap enrollment drift: 1 unenrolled principal(s)\". Today's 14:00 UTC audit run confirms the same single principal, `role/OrganizationAccountAccessRole`, for the 29th consecutive day. The audit Lambda's code is not in this repository (its deployment package is served from a Lambda-managed S3 snapshot), which is AC4 of this ticket. Related: the spend cap itself tripped today (`tripped_day: 2026-10-19`, the deny policy attached to Admin and the Gerrit/CI roles until 00:00 UTC); the org access role is unenrolled, so it is the one Bedrock-capable principal the cap does NOT deny while tripped, which is the concrete risk this drift report is about and the reason the enrol-or-accept decision (AC2) should not keep sliding."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1792429194845747828,"uuid":"efed12b5-0d0a-444f-b1b1-7d9fdcb89767"}